# crustify-audit artifacts — written into <repo>/crustify/audit/.
#
# The RECORD is meant to be committed: advisories, their reproducer SOURCES,
# leads, and the report are the deliverable, and an advisory is only worth
# anything if someone else can rebuild its reproduction. What is excluded here
# is everything a clean checkout regenerates.

# Deterministic scan output. Regenerate with `crustify-audit <repo> unsafe`.
/unsafe.json

# The agent's working area. Disposable by design and deleted between runs;
# a confirmed reproduction lives beside its advisory, never here.
/scratch/

# Cargo build trees under the reproducers. These dominate the directory —
# typically ~99% of its bytes — and hold rebuildable object files, static
# libcurl copies and incremental-compilation graphs.
**/target/
**/target-*/

# Uncomment to keep agent transcripts out of the history as well. They are the
# provenance for advisory attribution, so they are tracked by default.
# /logs/
